abstract: >-
  A beginner friendly lesson on spatial analysis in Python using Google Colab,
  written for social scientists. It covers road network analysis and travel
  time, spatial autocorrelation with PySAL, spatial clustering of point data,
  and NDVI from Landsat imagery. Each episode links to three short notebooks that read their
  data directly from the web.
